== Requirements and use ==

# Read the real project's release, build, scaffold and repository instructions.
# Select one version set and the shared workflows needed for the task.
# For core, read its actual AGENTS.md and local skills before the central adaptations.
# Inspect target APIs; preserve factories, transactions, role/client/org access and generated models.
# Review installation conflicts separately; no installation or publication is performed by this page.

An agent needs access to Markdown/resources. Python 3 and PyYAML validate the catalog. The local review helper uses Git 2.31+, Bash 3.2+ and local Git identity.

== Versions and validation ==

The target iDempiere line is not a skill release number. Per-skill SHA-256 revisions identify instructions and all resources in docs/skill-versions.json. Published releases require a deliberate tag. No release-tested status is inferred from a version folder.

<pre>
python3 scripts/validate_catalog.py
python3 scripts/catalog_versions.py --check
python3 tests/test_review_pr.py
</pre>

The adoption review records 78 entry validations and ten local Git fixture scenarios. Java compilation, OSGi activation, PackIn, PostgreSQL/Oracle and UI compatibility remain separate checks. Core migrations/AD IDs are generated by the developer through UI/Centralized IDs; private plugins follow their own policy.

